/-!
# Finiteness from exact tropical certificates

Lemma 6.18 of the paper (`lem:goodred`) shows that a coordinate ring over a local ring is a finite
module, from tropical data: a fan with support the tropical prevariety of a set `G` of
polynomials, and the absence of common zeros in the torus of the reduced initial forms on its
cones. Here the hypothesis is an exact certificate at every weight, and the valuative argument of
the paper is carried out.

## Setting

* `O` is a Noetherian local ring with maximal ideal `𝔪` and residue field `k = ResidueField O`.
  (The paper's `O` is a domain; this is not used.)
* `A = O[v_1, …, v_r]` is `MvPolynomial (Fin r) O` and `I ⊆ A` is an ideal.
* `ξ : Fin N → A`, each `ξ i` a unit modulo `I`, and each `v_j` congruent modulo `I` to a polynomial
  in the `ξ i` with coefficients in `O`.
* `G` is a finite set of polynomials in `MvPolynomial (Fin N) O` whose coefficients are all units
  of `O`, with `g(ξ) ∈ I` for every `g ∈ G`.

For an additive commutative group `Γ` and `w : Fin N → Γ`, the weight of an exponent `α` is
`tropWeight w α = ⟨α, w⟩ = ∑ i, α i • w i`. For a linear order on `Γ`, `initPattern w g` is the set
of exponents `α` in the support of `g` with `⟨α, w⟩` minimal, and `initForm w g = in_w(g) ∈ k[X]`
is the sum over the initial pattern of the residues of the coefficients times `X^α`.

The certificate hypothesis `TropCert G`: for every linearly ordered additive commutative group
`Γ` (in the universe of `O`) and every `w : Fin N → Γ` with some `w i < 0`, either some `g ∈ G` has
exactly one exponent in its initial pattern at `w`, or there are `a : ℕ` and cofactors
`c_g ∈ k[X]` with `(∏ i, X i) ^ a = ∑_{g ∈ G} c_g · in_w(g)`. For real weights, by the
Nullstellensatz, the second alternative at `w` is equivalent to the absence of common zeros of the
initial forms at `w` in the torus over an algebraic closure of `k`, which is the hypothesis of the
paper on the cone containing `w`. The first alternative says that `w` lies outside the tropical
prevariety of `G`; it implies the second (a monomial with a unit coefficient divides a power of
`∏ i, X i`) and is listed separately because it needs no cofactors.

## Main statements

* `goodred`: `A ⧸ I` is integral over `O`.
* `goodred_finite`: `A ⧸ I` is a finite `O`-module.
* `goodred_isIntegral_X`: each `v_j` is integral over `O` modulo `I`.

## Proof

* `exists_valuationSubring_of_not_isIntegral`: if `y` in a field `K` (an `O`-algebra) is not
  integral over `O`, the ideal `𝔪 · O[1/y] + (1/y)` of `O[1/y] ⊆ K` is proper, since a relation
  `1 = a_0 + a_1 y⁻¹ + ⋯ + a_n y⁻ⁿ` with `a_0 ∈ 𝔪` would make `y` integral (`1 - a_0` is a unit).
  A valuation subring `V` of `K` containing `O[1/y]` whose maximal ideal contains this ideal
  (`Ideal.image_subset_nonunits_valuationSubring`, from `LocalSubring.exists_le_valuationSubring`)
  has `v ≤ 1` on `O`, `v < 1` on `𝔪`, and `y ∉ V`.
* `isIntegral_mk_X_of_isPrime`: for a prime `𝔮 ⊇ I` and `y` the image of `v_j` in the fraction
  field `K` of `A ⧸ 𝔮`, suppose `y` is not integral over `O` and take `V` as above. The images `t i`
  of the `ξ i` are nonzero, every `g ∈ G` vanishes at `t`, and `v(t i) > 1` for some `i`, since
  otherwise `y`, a polynomial in the `t i` over `O`, would lie in `V`.
* `false_of_valuationSubring`: the contradiction. Let `Γ` be the group of units of the value group
  of `V`, written additively, and `w i = -log v(t i)` (the inverse of `v(t i)`); some `w i < 0`.
  The terms of `g(t)` have valuations given by the weights, since the coefficients are units.
  If the initial pattern of some `g ∈ G` is a single exponent, the term of least weight is strictly
  dominant, which contradicts `g(t) = 0`. Otherwise, the subgroup of `Γ` generated by the `w i` is
  free of finite rank (`exists_lift_of_isAddTorsionFree`), so there are `u i ∈ Kˣ` with
  `v(u i) = v(t i)` such that `u^α` depends only on `⟨α, w⟩`. The residues `y_i` of `t i / u i` in
  the residue field of `V` are nonzero. For `g ∈ G` with initial pattern `P ∋ α₀`, `in_w(g)(y)`
  (coefficients mapped through `k → ResidueField V`) is the residue of
  `(∑_{α ∈ P} c_α t^α) / u^{α₀} = -(∑_{α ∉ P} c_α t^α) / u^{α₀}`, which has valuation `< 1`; so
  `in_w(g)(y) = 0`. Evaluating the certificate at `y` gives `(∏ i, y_i) ^ a = 0`, a contradiction.
* `goodred_isIntegral_X`: `A` is Noetherian, so `I` has finitely many minimal primes. The product of
  monic relations of `v_j` modulo the minimal primes is monic and lies in their intersection, the
  radical of `I`; a power of it lies in `I`.

## Remarks

* The hypothesis quantifies over linearly ordered groups `Γ` in the universe of `O` because the
  value group of a valuation ring of the fraction field of a quotient of `A`, which need not be
  `ℤ` or `ℝ`, is used. (The paper uses a discrete valuation, which exists because the local ring
  is Noetherian, by EGA II 7.1.7; that theorem is not used here.)
-/

namespace CC6Full

open MvPolynomial IsLocalRing

noncomputable section

universe u

/-! ### Weights, initial patterns and initial forms -/

section Defs

variable {N : ℕ}

/-- The weight `⟨α, w⟩ = ∑ i, α i • w i` of an exponent vector `α` at `w`. -/
def tropWeight {Γ : Type*} [AddCommMonoid Γ] (w : Fin N → Γ) (α : Fin N →₀ ℕ) : Γ :=
  ∑ i, α i • w i

/-- The initial pattern of `g` at `w`: the exponents `α` in the support of `g` at which the
weight `⟨α, w⟩` is minimal. -/
def initPattern {R Γ : Type*} [CommSemiring R] [AddCommMonoid Γ] [LinearOrder Γ]
    (w : Fin N → Γ) (g : MvPolynomial (Fin N) R) : Finset (Fin N →₀ ℕ) :=
  {α ∈ g.support | ∀ β ∈ g.support, tropWeight w α ≤ tropWeight w β}

/-- The initial form `in_w(g)` of `g` at `w`, with the coefficients reduced to the residue field
of the local ring `O`: the sum of the terms of `g` whose exponents lie in the initial pattern. -/
def initForm {O Γ : Type*} [CommRing O] [IsLocalRing O] [AddCommMonoid Γ] [LinearOrder Γ]
    (w : Fin N → Γ) (g : MvPolynomial (Fin N) O) : MvPolynomial (Fin N) (ResidueField O) :=
  ∑ α ∈ initPattern w g, monomial α (residue O (g.coeff α))

/-- The certificate hypothesis for a finite set `G` of polynomials over the local ring `O`: for
every linearly ordered additive commutative group `Γ` (in the universe of `O`) and every
`w : Fin N → Γ` with some `w i < 0`, either some `g ∈ G` has a single exponent in its initial
pattern at `w`, or some power of `∏ i, X i` is a combination of the initial forms of the
elements of `G` at `w`, with cofactors over the residue field. -/
def TropCert {O : Type u} [CommRing O] [IsLocalRing O] (G : Finset (MvPolynomial (Fin N) O)) :
    Prop :=
  ∀ (Γ : Type u) [AddCommGroup Γ] [LinearOrder Γ] [IsOrderedAddMonoid Γ] (w : Fin N → Γ),
    (∃ i, w i < 0) →
      (∃ g ∈ G, (initPattern w g).card = 1) ∨
        ∃ (a : ℕ) (c : MvPolynomial (Fin N) O → MvPolynomial (Fin N) (ResidueField O)),
          (∏ i, X i) ^ a = ∑ g ∈ G, c g * initForm w g

lemma mem_initPattern {R Γ : Type*} [CommSemiring R] [AddCommMonoid Γ] [LinearOrder Γ]
    {w : Fin N → Γ} {g : MvPolynomial (Fin N) R} {α : Fin N →₀ ℕ} :
    α ∈ initPattern w g ↔ α ∈ g.support ∧ ∀ β ∈ g.support, tropWeight w α ≤ tropWeight w β :=
  Finset.mem_filter

end Defs

/-! ### Lifting finitely generated subgroups of torsion-free groups -/

/-- Let `ν : M → Γ` be a surjective homomorphism of abelian groups with `Γ` torsion-free, and
`w : ι → Γ` a finite family. Then the `w i` have lifts `u i` such that `∑ i, a i • u i` depends
only on `∑ i, a i • w i`. (The subgroup generated by the `w i` is free of finite rank, so the
inclusion lifts along `ν`.) -/
theorem exists_lift_of_isAddTorsionFree {M Γ ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] [AddCommGroup M]
    [AddCommGroup Γ] [IsAddTorsionFree Γ] (ν : M →+ Γ) (hν : Function.Surjective ν)
    (w : ι → Γ) :
    ∃ u : ι → M, (∀ i, ν (u i) = w i) ∧
      ∀ a b : ι → ℕ, ∑ i, a i • w i = ∑ i, b i • w i → ∑ i, a i • u i = ∑ i, b i • u i := by
  let H : Submodule ℤ Γ := Submodule.span ℤ (Set.range w)
  have : Module.Finite ℤ H := Module.Finite.span_of_finite ℤ (Set.finite_range w)
  have : Module.IsTorsionFree ℤ H :=
    Function.Injective.moduleIsTorsionFree (R := ℤ) (fun x : H => (x : Γ)) Subtype.val_injective
      (fun _ _ => rfl)
  have : Module.Free ℤ H := Module.free_of_finite_type_torsion_free'
  obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := Module.projective_lifting_property ν.toIntLinearMap H.subtype hν
  have hw : ∀ i, w i ∈ H := fun i => Submodule.subset_span ⟨i, rfl⟩
  have hsum : ∀ a : ι → ℕ, ∑ i, a i • s ⟨w i, hw i⟩ = s (∑ i, a i • ⟨w i, hw i⟩) := by
    intro a
    simp only [map_sum, map_nsmul]
  have hcoe : ∀ a : ι → ℕ, ((∑ i, a i • ⟨w i, hw i⟩ : H) : Γ) = ∑ i, a i • w i := by
    intro a
    simp
  refine ⟨fun i => s ⟨w i, hw i⟩, fun i => ?_, fun a b hab => ?_⟩
  · exact LinearMap.congr_fun hs ⟨w i, hw i⟩
  · rw [hsum a, hsum b]
    congr 1
    exact Subtype.ext (by rw [hcoe, hcoe, hab])

/-! ### The additive valuation of a valuation subring -/

section Valuation

variable {K : Type*} [Field K] (V : ValuationSubring K)

/-- The additive valuation of `V` on `Kˣ`, with values in the units of the value group written
additively: `x ↦ v(x)⁻¹`. The inverse turns the multiplicative convention (`v ≤ 1` on `V`) into
the additive one (`≥ 0` on `V`). -/
def addVal : Additive Kˣ →+ Additive V.ValueGroupˣ :=
  MonoidHom.toAdditive (Units.map (V.valuation : K →* V.ValueGroup))⁻¹

lemma addVal_ofMul (x : Kˣ) :
    addVal V (Additive.ofMul x) =
      Additive.ofMul (Units.map (V.valuation : K →* V.ValueGroup) x)⁻¹ := rfl

lemma addVal_le_iff (x y : Kˣ) :
    addVal V (Additive.ofMul x) ≤ addVal V (Additive.ofMul y) ↔
      V.valuation (y : K) ≤ V.valuation (x : K) := by
  rw [addVal_ofMul, addVal_ofMul, Additive.ofMul_le, inv_le_inv_iff, ← Units.val_le_val,
    Units.coe_map, Units.coe_map]
  rfl

lemma addVal_lt_iff (x y : Kˣ) :
    addVal V (Additive.ofMul x) < addVal V (Additive.ofMul y) ↔
      V.valuation (y : K) < V.valuation (x : K) := by
  rw [← not_le, addVal_le_iff, not_le]

lemma addVal_surjective : Function.Surjective (addVal V) := by
  intro γ
  obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ :=
    V.valuation_surjective (((Additive.toMul γ)⁻¹ : V.ValueGroupˣ) : V.ValueGroup)
  have hz0 : z ≠ 0 := by
    rintro rfl
    rw [map_zero] at hz
    exact Units.ne_zero _ hz.symm
  refine ⟨Additive.ofMul (Units.mk0 z hz0), ?_⟩
  have : Units.map (V.valuation : K →* V.ValueGroup) (Units.mk0 z hz0) = (Additive.toMul γ)⁻¹ :=
    Units.ext (by simpa using hz)
  rw [addVal_ofMul, this, inv_inv]
  rfl

end Valuation

/-! ### A valuation ring centred on the maximal ideal and negative at a non-integral element -/

/-- If `y ∈ K` is not integral over the local ring `O`, there is a valuation subring `V` of `K`
that contains the image of `O`, on which the image of the maximal ideal of `O` has valuation
`< 1`, and which does not contain `y`. -/
theorem exists_valuationSubring_of_not_isIntegral {O K : Type*} [CommRing O] [IsLocalRing O]
    [Field K] [Algebra O K] {y : K} (hy : ¬ IsIntegral O y) :
    ∃ V : ValuationSubring K, (∀ a, algebraMap O K a ∈ V) ∧
      (∀ a ∈ maximalIdeal O, V.valuation (algebraMap O K a) < 1) ∧ y ∉ V := by
  have hy0 : y ≠ 0 := by
    rintro rfl
    exact hy isIntegral_zero
  let := invertibleOfNonzero hy0
  let B := Algebra.adjoin O {y⁻¹}
  let xB : B := ⟨y⁻¹, Algebra.subset_adjoin rfl⟩
  have hJ : (maximalIdeal O).map (algebraMap O B) ⊔ Ideal.span {xB} ≠ ⊤ := by
    intro h
    obtain ⟨p, hp, hpx⟩ := Algebra.exists_aeval_invOf_eq_zero_of_idealMap_adjoin_sup_span_eq_top
      y⁻¹ (maximalIdeal O) (maximalIdeal.isMaximal O).ne_top h
    have H : IsUnit p.leadingCoeff := of_not_not fun h => by simpa using sub_mem h hp
    have hmon : (Polynomial.C (↑H.unit⁻¹ : O) * p).Monic :=
      Polynomial.monic_C_mul_of_mul_leadingCoeff_eq_one H.val_inv_mul
    exact hy ⟨_, hmon, by simpa using .inr hpx⟩
  obtain ⟨V, hBV, hJV⟩ := Ideal.image_subset_nonunits_valuationSubring (A := B.toSubring) _ hJ
  refine ⟨V, fun a => hBV (B.algebraMap_mem a), fun a ha => ?_, ?_⟩
  · exact V.mem_nonunits_iff.1
      (hJV ⟨algebraMap O B a, Ideal.mem_sup_left (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ ha), rfl⟩)
  · exact (V.inv_mem_nonunits_iff.1
      (hJV ⟨xB, Ideal.mem_sup_right (Ideal.subset_span rfl), rfl⟩)).resolve_left hy0

/-! ### The tropical argument -/

/-- The valuative core of `goodred`. Let `V` be a valuation subring of a field `K` dominating
the local ring `O` (through an `O`-algebra structure on `K`), and let `t : Fin N → K` be nonzero
with `v(t i) > 1` for some `i`, at which every `g ∈ G` vanishes, where the coefficients of each
`g ∈ G` are units. Then the certificate hypothesis fails. -/
theorem false_of_valuationSubring {O K : Type u} [CommRing O] [IsLocalRing O] [Field K]
    [Algebra O K] (V : ValuationSubring K) (hO : ∀ a, algebraMap O K a ∈ V)
    (hm : ∀ a ∈ maximalIdeal O, V.valuation (algebraMap O K a) < 1)
    {N : ℕ} (t : Fin N → K) (ht : ∀ i, t i ≠ 0) (hneg : ∃ i, 1 < V.valuation (t i))
    (G : Finset (MvPolynomial (Fin N) O)) (hG : ∀ g ∈ G, ∀ α ∈ g.support, IsUnit (g.coeff α))
    (hGt : ∀ g ∈ G, aeval t g = 0) (hcert : TropCert G) : False := by
  classical
  -- the local homomorphism `O → V`
  let φ : O →+* V := (algebraMap O K).codRestrict V hO
  have : IsLocalHom φ := ⟨fun a ha => by
    by_contra hna
    have h1 := hm a ((mem_maximalIdeal a).2 (mem_nonunits_iff.2 hna))
    exact mem_nonunits_iff.1 ((mem_maximalIdeal _).1 ((V.valuation_lt_one_iff (φ a)).2 h1)) ha⟩
  have hcv : ∀ g ∈ G, ∀ α ∈ g.support, V.valuation (algebraMap O K (g.coeff α)) = 1 :=
    fun g hg α hα => (V.valuation_eq_one_iff (φ (g.coeff α))).1 ((hG g hg α hα).map φ)
  -- the values of the monomials
  let tp : (Fin N →₀ ℕ) → K := fun α => ∏ i, t i ^ α i
  have htp0 : ∀ α, V.valuation (tp α) ≠ 0 := fun α =>
    (Valuation.ne_zero_iff _).2 (Finset.prod_ne_zero_iff.2 fun i _ => pow_ne_zero _ (ht i))
  have haeval : ∀ g : MvPolynomial (Fin N) O,
      aeval t g = ∑ α ∈ g.support, algebraMap O K (g.coeff α) * tp α := fun g => by
    rw [aeval_def, eval₂_eq']
  -- the weights
  let tu : Fin N → Kˣ := fun i => Units.mk0 (t i) (ht i)
  let w : Fin N → Additive V.ValueGroupˣ := fun i => addVal V (Additive.ofMul (tu i))
  have hwt : ∀ α, tropWeight w α = addVal V (Additive.ofMul (∏ i, tu i ^ α i)) := fun α => by
    simp only [tropWeight, w, ofMul_prod, ofMul_pow, map_sum, map_nsmul]
  have htu : ∀ α : Fin N →₀ ℕ, ((∏ i, tu i ^ α i : Kˣ) : K) = tp α := fun α => by
    simp [tu, tp, Units.coe_prod]
  have hwlt : ∀ α β, tropWeight w α < tropWeight w β ↔
      V.valuation (tp β) < V.valuation (tp α) := fun α β => by
    rw [hwt, hwt, addVal_lt_iff, htu, htu]
  have hneg' : ∃ i, w i < 0 := by
    obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := hneg
    refine ⟨i, ?_⟩
    have h0 : (0 : Additive V.ValueGroupˣ) = addVal V (Additive.ofMul 1) := by simp
    rw [h0, addVal_lt_iff]
    simpa [tu] using hi
  rcases hcert _ w hneg' with ⟨g, hg, hcard⟩ | ⟨a, c, hc⟩
  · -- a single exponent in the initial pattern: the term of least weight cannot cancel
    obtain ⟨α₀, hα₀⟩ := Finset.card_eq_one.1 hcard
    have hmem : α₀ ∈ initPattern w g := hα₀ ▸ Finset.mem_singleton_self α₀
    obtain ⟨hα₀s, hmin⟩ := mem_initPattern.1 hmem
    have hlt : ∀ β ∈ g.support, β ≠ α₀ → V.valuation (tp β) < V.valuation (tp α₀) := by
      intro β hβ hne
      have hβP : β ∉ initPattern w g := by
        rw [hα₀]
        simpa using hne
      rw [mem_initPattern] at hβP
      push Not at hβP
      obtain ⟨γ, hγ, hγβ⟩ := hβP hβ
      exact (hwlt _ _).1 ((hmin γ hγ).trans_lt hγβ)
    have hrest : V.valuation (∑ β ∈ g.support.erase α₀, algebraMap O K (g.coeff β) * tp β) <
        V.valuation (algebraMap O K (g.coeff α₀) * tp α₀) := by
      rw [map_mul, hcv g hg α₀ hα₀s, one_mul]
      refine Valuation.map_sum_lt _ (htp0 α₀) fun β hβ => ?_
      obtain ⟨hne, hβs⟩ := Finset.mem_erase.1 hβ
      rw [map_mul, hcv g hg β hβs, one_mul]
      exact hlt β hβs hne
    have h := Valuation.map_add_eq_of_lt_left _ hrest
    rw [Finset.add_sum_erase _ (fun β => algebraMap O K (g.coeff β) * tp β) hα₀s, ← haeval,
      hGt g hg, map_zero, map_mul, hcv g hg α₀ hα₀s, one_mul] at h
    exact htp0 α₀ h.symm
  · -- a monomial in the ideal of the initial forms: evaluate at the residues of `t i / u i`
    obtain ⟨u, hu, hu'⟩ := exists_lift_of_isAddTorsionFree (addVal V) (addVal_surjective V) w
    let uu : Fin N → Kˣ := fun i => Additive.toMul (u i)
    have huv : ∀ i, V.valuation (uu i : K) = V.valuation (t i) := fun i => by
      have h' : addVal V (Additive.ofMul (uu i)) = addVal V (Additive.ofMul (tu i)) := hu i
      have h1 := (addVal_le_iff V _ _).1 h'.le
      have h2 := (addVal_le_iff V _ _).1 h'.ge
      simp only [tu, Units.val_mk0] at h1 h2
      exact le_antisymm h2 h1
    let UU : (Fin N →₀ ℕ) → Kˣ := fun α => ∏ i, uu i ^ α i
    have hUUsum : ∀ α, UU α = Additive.toMul (∑ i, α i • u i) := fun α => by
      simp only [UU, uu, toMul_sum, toMul_nsmul]
    have hUU : ∀ α β, tropWeight w α = tropWeight w β → UU α = UU β := fun α β h => by
      rw [hUUsum, hUUsum, hu' α β h]
    have hUUv : ∀ α, V.valuation (UU α : K) = V.valuation (tp α) := fun α => by
      simp only [UU, tp, Units.coe_prod, Units.val_pow_eq_pow_val, map_prod, map_pow, huv]
    have hq1 : ∀ i, V.valuation (t i * ((uu i : K))⁻¹) = 1 := fun i => by
      rw [map_mul, map_inv₀, huv i, mul_inv_cancel₀ ((Valuation.ne_zero_iff _).2 (ht i))]
    let q : Fin N → V := fun i => ⟨t i * ((uu i : K))⁻¹, (V.valuation_le_one_iff _).1 (hq1 i).le⟩
    have hqu : ∀ i, IsUnit (q i) := fun i => (V.valuation_eq_one_iff (q i)).2 (hq1 i)
    let ψ := ResidueField.map φ
    let y : Fin N → ResidueField V := fun i => residue V (q i)
    have hy0 : ∀ i, y i ≠ 0 := fun i => (residue_ne_zero_iff_isUnit _).2 (hqu i)
    have hin : ∀ g ∈ G, eval₂Hom ψ y (initForm w g) = 0 := by
      intro g hg
      have h1 : eval₂Hom ψ y (initForm w g) =
          residue V (∑ α ∈ initPattern w g, φ (g.coeff α) * ∏ i, q i ^ α i) := by
        simp only [initForm, map_sum, eval₂Hom_monomial, Finsupp.prod_pow, ψ,
          ResidueField.map_residue, y, map_mul, map_prod, map_pow]
      rw [h1, residue_eq_zero_iff, V.valuation_lt_one_iff]
      have h2 : ((∑ α ∈ initPattern w g, φ (g.coeff α) * ∏ i, q i ^ α i : V) : K) =
          ∑ α ∈ initPattern w g, algebraMap O K (g.coeff α) * (tp α * ((UU α : Kˣ) : K)⁻¹) := by
        push_cast
        refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun α _ => ?_
        simp [q, φ, tp, UU, mul_pow, Finset.prod_mul_distrib, Units.coe_prod, inv_pow,
          Finset.prod_inv_distrib]
      rw [h2]
      rcases (initPattern w g).eq_empty_or_nonempty with hP | ⟨α₀, hα₀⟩
      · rw [hP, Finset.sum_empty, map_zero]
        exact zero_lt_one
      obtain ⟨hα₀s, hmin⟩ := mem_initPattern.1 hα₀
      have h3 : ∑ α ∈ initPattern w g, algebraMap O K (g.coeff α) * (tp α * ((UU α : Kˣ) : K)⁻¹) =
          (∑ α ∈ initPattern w g, algebraMap O K (g.coeff α) * tp α) * ((UU α₀ : Kˣ) : K)⁻¹ := by
        rw [Finset.sum_mul]
        refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun α hα => ?_
        obtain ⟨hαs, hminα⟩ := mem_initPattern.1 hα
        rw [hUU α α₀ (le_antisymm (hminα α₀ hα₀s) (hmin α hαs)), mul_assoc]
      have h4 : ∑ α ∈ initPattern w g, algebraMap O K (g.coeff α) * tp α =
          -∑ α ∈ g.support with ¬ ∀ β ∈ g.support, tropWeight w α ≤ tropWeight w β,
            algebraMap O K (g.coeff α) * tp α := by
        have h0 := hGt g hg
        rw [haeval, ← Finset.sum_filter_add_sum_filter_not g.support
          (fun α => ∀ β ∈ g.support, tropWeight w α ≤ tropWeight w β)] at h0
        exact eq_neg_of_add_eq_zero_left h0
      rw [h3, h4, map_mul, Valuation.map_neg, map_inv₀, hUUv α₀]
      have h5 : V.valuation (∑ α ∈ g.support with ¬ ∀ β ∈ g.support,
          tropWeight w α ≤ tropWeight w β, algebraMap O K (g.coeff α) * tp α) <
          V.valuation (tp α₀) := by
        refine Valuation.map_sum_lt _ (htp0 α₀) fun β hβ => ?_
        obtain ⟨hβs, hβn⟩ := Finset.mem_filter.1 hβ
        push Not at hβn
        obtain ⟨γ, hγ, hγβ⟩ := hβn
        rw [map_mul, hcv g hg β hβs, one_mul]
        exact (hwlt _ _).1 ((hmin γ hγ).trans_lt hγβ)
      calc _ < V.valuation (tp α₀) * (V.valuation (tp α₀))⁻¹ :=
            mul_lt_mul_of_pos_right h5 (inv_pos.2 (zero_lt_iff.2 (htp0 α₀)))
        _ = 1 := mul_inv_cancel₀ (htp0 α₀)
    have h := congrArg (eval₂Hom ψ y) hc
    rw [map_pow, map_prod, map_sum,
      Finset.sum_eq_zero fun g hg => by rw [map_mul, hin g hg, mul_zero]] at h
    simp only [eval₂Hom_X'] at h
    exact pow_ne_zero a (Finset.prod_ne_zero_iff.2 fun i _ => hy0 i) h

/-! ### Integrality modulo a prime, and modulo `I` -/

section Main

variable {O : Type u} [CommRing O] [IsLocalRing O] {r N : ℕ}

/-- Under the hypotheses of `goodred`, each variable is integral over `O` modulo every prime
ideal containing `I`. -/
theorem isIntegral_mk_X_of_isPrime {I : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin r) O)}
    {ξ : Fin N → MvPolynomial (Fin r) O} (hξ : ∀ i, IsUnit (Ideal.Quotient.mk I (ξ i)))
    (hX : ∀ j, ∃ p : MvPolynomial (Fin N) O, X j - aeval ξ p ∈ I)
    {G : Finset (MvPolynomial (Fin N) O)} (hG : ∀ g ∈ G, ∀ α ∈ g.support, IsUnit (g.coeff α))
    (hGI : ∀ g ∈ G, aeval ξ g ∈ I) (hcert : TropCert G)
    (𝔮 : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin r) O)) [𝔮.IsPrime] (hI : I ≤ 𝔮) (j : Fin r) :
    IsIntegral O (Ideal.Quotient.mk 𝔮 (X j)) := by
  by_contra hnot
  let R' := MvPolynomial (Fin r) O ⧸ 𝔮
  let K := FractionRing R'
  let ι : R' →ₐ[O] K := IsScalarTower.toAlgHom O R' K
  have hι : Function.Injective ι := IsFractionRing.injective R' K
  let Φ : MvPolynomial (Fin r) O →ₐ[O] K := ι.comp (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ O 𝔮)
  have hΦ : ∀ a, Φ a = ι (Ideal.Quotient.mk 𝔮 a) := fun _ => rfl
  have hΦI : ∀ a ∈ I, Φ a = 0 := fun a ha => by
    rw [hΦ, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.2 (hI ha), map_zero]
  have hy : ¬ IsIntegral O (Φ (X j)) := by
    rwa [hΦ, isIntegral_algHom_iff ι hι]
  obtain ⟨V, hO, hm, hyV⟩ := exists_valuationSubring_of_not_isIntegral hy
  let t : Fin N → K := fun i => Φ (ξ i)
  have ht : ∀ i, t i ≠ 0 := fun i => by
    have hu : IsUnit (Ideal.Quotient.mk 𝔮 (ξ i)) := by
      simpa [Ideal.Quotient.factor_mk] using (hξ i).map (Ideal.Quotient.factor hI)
    exact (hu.map ι).ne_zero
  have haeval : ∀ p : MvPolynomial (Fin N) O, Φ (aeval ξ p) = aeval t p := fun p =>
    comp_aeval_apply ξ Φ p
  have hGt : ∀ g ∈ G, aeval t g = 0 := fun g hg => by
    rw [← haeval]
    exact hΦI _ (hGI g hg)
  have hneg : ∃ i, 1 < V.valuation (t i) := by
    by_contra hcon
    push Not at hcon
    have htV : ∀ i, t i ∈ V := fun i => (V.valuation_le_one_iff _).1 (hcon i)
    have hmemV : ∀ p : MvPolynomial (Fin N) O, aeval t p ∈ V := by
      intro p
      induction p using MvPolynomial.induction_on with
      | C a => simpa using hO a
      | add p q hp hq => rw [map_add]; exact add_mem hp hq
      | mul_X p i hp => rw [map_mul, aeval_X]; exact mul_mem hp (htV i)
    obtain ⟨p, hp⟩ := hX j
    have hXp : Φ (X j) = aeval t p := by
      have := hΦI _ hp
      rwa [map_sub, sub_eq_zero, haeval] at this
    exact hyV (hXp ▸ hmemV p)
  exact false_of_valuationSubring V hO hm t ht hneg G hG hGt hcert

variable [IsNoetherianRing O]

/-- Under the hypotheses of `goodred`, each variable is integral over `O` modulo `I`. -/
theorem goodred_isIntegral_X (I : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin r) O))
    (ξ : Fin N → MvPolynomial (Fin r) O) (hξ : ∀ i, IsUnit (Ideal.Quotient.mk I (ξ i)))
    (hX : ∀ j, ∃ p : MvPolynomial (Fin N) O, X j - aeval ξ p ∈ I)
    (G : Finset (MvPolynomial (Fin N) O)) (hG : ∀ g ∈ G, ∀ α ∈ g.support, IsUnit (g.coeff α))
    (hGI : ∀ g ∈ G, aeval ξ g ∈ I) (hcert : TropCert G) (j : Fin r) :
    IsIntegral O (Ideal.Quotient.mk I (X j)) := by
  classical
  have hfin := Ideal.finite_minimalPrimes_of_isNoetherianRing (MvPolynomial (Fin r) O) I
  have hq : ∀ 𝔮 ∈ I.minimalPrimes, ∃ f : Polynomial O,
      f.Monic ∧ Polynomial.aeval (X j : MvPolynomial (Fin r) O) f ∈ 𝔮 := by
    intro 𝔮 h𝔮
    have : 𝔮.IsPrime := h𝔮.1.1
    obtain ⟨f, hfm, hf⟩ := isIntegral_mk_X_of_isPrime hξ hX hG hGI hcert 𝔮 h𝔮.1.2 j
    refine ⟨f, hfm, ?_⟩
    rw [← Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem, ← Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ_eq_mk O,
      ← Polynomial.aeval_algHom_apply, Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ_eq_mk O, Polynomial.aeval_def]
    exact hf
  choose! f hfm hf using hq
  let F : Polynomial O := ∏ 𝔮 ∈ hfin.toFinset, f 𝔮
  have hFm : F.Monic :=
    Polynomial.monic_prod_of_monic _ _ fun 𝔮 h𝔮 => hfm 𝔮 (hfin.mem_toFinset.1 h𝔮)
  have hFrad : Polynomial.aeval (X j : MvPolynomial (Fin r) O) F ∈ I.radical := by
    rw [← Ideal.sInf_minimalPrimes, Ideal.mem_sInf]
    intro 𝔮 h𝔮
    rw [map_prod, ← Finset.mul_prod_erase _ _ (hfin.mem_toFinset.2 h𝔮)]
    exact Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ (hf 𝔮 h𝔮)
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := hFrad
  refine ⟨F ^ n, hFm.pow n, ?_⟩
  rw [← Polynomial.aeval_def, ← Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ_eq_mk O, Polynomial.aeval_algHom_apply,
    map_pow, Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ_eq_mk O, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem]
  exact hn

/-- **Finiteness from exact tropical certificates** (Lemma 6.18 of the paper, `lem:goodred`, with
an exact certificate as hypothesis). Let `O` be a Noetherian local ring, `I` an ideal of
`A = O[v_1, …, v_r]`, and `ξ : Fin N → A` with each `ξ i` a unit modulo `I` and each `v_j`
congruent modulo `I` to a polynomial in the `ξ i` over `O`. Let `G` be a finite set of polynomials
over `O` whose coefficients are units, with `g(ξ) ∈ I` for `g ∈ G`, satisfying the certificate
hypothesis `TropCert G`. Then `A ⧸ I` is integral over `O`. -/
theorem goodred (I : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin r) O))
    (ξ : Fin N → MvPolynomial (Fin r) O) (hξ : ∀ i, IsUnit (Ideal.Quotient.mk I (ξ i)))
    (hX : ∀ j, ∃ p : MvPolynomial (Fin N) O, X j - aeval ξ p ∈ I)
    (G : Finset (MvPolynomial (Fin N) O)) (hG : ∀ g ∈ G, ∀ α ∈ g.support, IsUnit (g.coeff α))
    (hGI : ∀ g ∈ G, aeval ξ g ∈ I) (hcert : TropCert G) :
    Algebra.IsIntegral O (MvPolynomial (Fin r) O ⧸ I) := by
  refine ⟨fun x => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨p, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective x
  induction p using MvPolynomial.induction_on with
  | C a => exact isIntegral_algebraMap (R := O) (x := a)
  | add p q hp hq => rw [map_add]; exact hp.add hq
  | mul_X p j hp => rw [map_mul]; exact hp.mul (goodred_isIntegral_X I ξ hξ hX G hG hGI hcert j)

/-- Under the hypotheses of `goodred`, `O[v] ⧸ I` is a finite `O`-module. -/
theorem goodred_finite (I : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin r) O))
    (ξ : Fin N → MvPolynomial (Fin r) O) (hξ : ∀ i, IsUnit (Ideal.Quotient.mk I (ξ i)))
    (hX : ∀ j, ∃ p : MvPolynomial (Fin N) O, X j - aeval ξ p ∈ I)
    (G : Finset (MvPolynomial (Fin N) O)) (hG : ∀ g ∈ G, ∀ α ∈ g.support, IsUnit (g.coeff α))
    (hGI : ∀ g ∈ G, aeval ξ g ∈ I) (hcert : TropCert G) :
    Module.Finite O (MvPolynomial (Fin r) O ⧸ I) := by
  have := goodred I ξ hξ hX G hG hGI hcert
  have : Algebra.FiniteType O (MvPolynomial (Fin r) O ⧸ I) :=
    Algebra.FiniteType.of_surjective (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ O I) (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ_surjective O I)
  exact Algebra.IsIntegral.finite

end Main

